  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Performance and Quality Analysis</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DFAT Performance and Quality Analysis:  Activities include annual independent validation of Final Investment Monitoring Reports (FIMR)s (and previously Final Aid Quality Checks - FAQCs) from 2019-2023. 

FIMRs are the final records of performance of DFAT aid investments of $3 million and over. DFAT-validated FIMR ratings are used to report to the Parliament and the public. FIMR validation is a core way DFAT fulfils its mandate to quality assure and verify aid performance data.  The outcomes of the investment are transparency of public reporting and the maintenance of an effective aid investment performance system that serves accountability, performance and risk management functions, and provides a structured process for assessing the impact of Australian aid investments.</narrative>
  </description>
